# Paint Application Extended — TSIS 2

Extended Paint app building on Practice 10 and Practice 11, using only Pygame's built-in capabilities.

## Repository Structure

```
TSIS2/
├── paint.py      # Main application — window, toolbar, event loop, Ctrl+S save
├── tools.py      # All drawing tool classes + flood-fill helper
└── assets/       # (reserved for icons / custom fonts if added later)
```

## Features Added (TSIS 2)

| Feature | Where |
|---|---|
| Pencil — freehand drawing with round caps | `tools.py → PencilTool` |
| Straight line with live preview | `tools.py → LineTool` |
| Three brush sizes (2 / 5 / 10 px) | `paint.py` + all tools |
| Flood-fill (BFS, exact color match) | `tools.py → FillTool / _flood_fill` |
| Ctrl+S save as timestamped PNG | `paint.py → save_canvas()` |
| Text tool — click, type, Enter/Esc | `tools.py → TextTool` |
| All Practice 10–11 shapes respect brush size | `tools.py → *Tool._draw(size)` |

> **Not re-implemented:** Rectangle, Circle, Eraser (Practice 10); Square, Right Triangle, Equilateral Triangle, Rhombus (Practice 11) — they are extended with brush-size support only.

## Setup

```bash
pip install pygame
python paint.py
```

Requires Python 3.10+ and Pygame 2.x.

## Controls

| Action | Input |
|---|---|
| Pencil | `P` or toolbar button |
| Line | `L` |
| Fill | `F` |
| Text | `T` |
| Eraser | `E` |
| Rectangle | `R` |
| Circle | `C` |
| Square | `S` |
| Right Triangle | `G` |
| Equilateral Triangle | `Q` |
| Rhombus | `H` |
| Brush small (2 px) | `1` or **S** button |
| Brush medium (5 px) | `2` or **M** button |
| Brush large (10 px) | `3` or **L** button |
| Pick color | Click palette swatch (bottom bar) |
| Save canvas | `Ctrl+S` → `canvas_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.png` |

## Architecture

### `tools.py`

- **`BaseTool`** — common interface: `on_mouse_down`, `on_mouse_move`, `on_mouse_up`, `draw_preview`
- **`_DragShapeTool`** — base for all click-drag shapes; stores start point, calls `_draw()` on release and in preview
- **`_flood_fill(surface, start, color)`** — standalone BFS function, used by `FillTool`; iterates with a `deque`, uses `get_at` / `set_at`, stops at color boundaries
- **`TextTool`** — maintains `active`, `buffer`, and `pos`; `handle_key()` is called from the main event loop; blinking cursor via `get_ticks() // 500 % 2`
- **`build_tool_registry()`** — returns `{name: instance}` dict consumed by `paint.py`

### `paint.py`

- Canvas is a `pygame.Surface` separate from the screen, blit onto it each frame
- Preview overlay is drawn directly on the screen (not the canvas), so live shape previews disappear cleanly each frame
- Status messages (save confirmation) auto-dismiss after 3 seconds
- Toolbar, canvas, and palette are stacked vertically: 56 px toolbar → canvas → 48 px palette